Bloodydeathworld.com

==English==

Imagine waking up in an bloody red room… you’re first thought would be 

“how did I get here?” 

You get up from the bloody stained bed.. and stubble and sway as you walk. You feel dizzy of course, but why??? 

You walk until you find your way in the hallway. Finally your legs give up and you fall on the hard unstable floor….. 

you get up and see blood and maggots on your hands, you scream and run. 

As you’re running you feel as if you been running around for hours… you make it to the end of the hallway, finally you pass out.

===Etymology===
1994, {{compound|en|Web|page}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A single [[hypertext]] document (transmitted as [[HTML]]) on the [[World Wide Web]], often [[hyperlink]]ed to others, and intended to be viewed with a [[web browser]].
#* '''2007''', Doug Rich, “How to Search for Supernovae”, in ''Astronomy'', v 35, n 3 (March), pp 70–72:
#*: Dave Bishop, an amateur astronomer, operates a supernova '''web page''' at www.rochesterastronomy.org/supernova.html, which lists new discoveries, including images.
# {{lb|en|loosely}} A [[website]], by extension from the [[home page]] of the site.
#: ''Be sure to check out my '''web page''' on the Internet when you get home.''

